<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{localization.locale}}">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{{page.title}}</title>
    {{#page.description}}<meta name="description" content="{{page.description}}">{{/page.description}}
{{!Mustache concatenates by juxtaposition, so an absolute URL needs no filter:
    shop.url is the origin, page.path is this page. The pair matters on a
    multi-locale site, where / and /en serve near-identical pages.}}
    <link rel="canonical" href="{{shop.url}}{{page.path}}">
    <meta property="og:type" content="website">
    <meta property="og:url" content="{{shop.url}}{{page.path}}">
    <meta property="og:title" content="{{page.title}}">
    {{#page.description}}<meta property="og:description" content="{{page.description}}">{{/page.description}}
    {{#page.ogImageUrl}}<meta property="og:image" content="{{page.ogImageUrl}}">{{/page.ogImageUrl}}
</head>
<body>
{{!The logo is shop.brand.logo — Shopify's shop object has no logo of its own.
    Inside the section, url is the image's; routes and shop resolve through the
    parent-context fallback, which is on because standards mode is off. The alt
    is the shop's name, as Dawn's header does: the image's own alt is null on
    every row until there is a write path for it.
    The section hugs its markup, same rule as the footer below: on its own line
    it is not standalone, so an operator with no logo ships the indentation of
    the line the tag sat on.
    NB a comment ends at the first close-brace pair, so it may not quote a tag.}}
    <header>{{#shop.brand.logo}}
        <a href="{{routes.root}}"><img src="{{url}}" alt="{{shop.name}}"></a>{{/shop.brand.logo}}
        <nav>{{#localization.languages}}{{#current}}<span lang="{{code}}">{{code}}</span>{{/current}}{{^current}}<a href="{{url}}" lang="{{code}}">{{code}}</a>{{/current}}{{/localization.languages}}</nav>
    </header>
{{!A page's block tags hug its markup on purpose: whitespace between a block tag
    and the content it holds is whitespace in the rendered page.}}
{{$content}}{{/content}}
    <footer>
{{!Each optional line opens its section at the end of the line before it, so an
    operator who publishes neither emits nothing here rather than two blank
    lines. Same hugging rule as the content block above.}}
        <p>{{shop.address}}</p>{{#shop.phone}}
        <p><a href="tel:{{shop.phone}}">{{shop.phone}}</a></p>{{/shop.phone}}{{#shop.email}}
        <p><a href="mailto:{{shop.email}}">{{shop.email}}</a></p>{{/shop.email}}
    </footer>
</body>
</html>
